technical sharing; and non-commercial copying, modification and redistribution.
Copies and distributions must retain this license and copyright notice, identify
modifications, and must not imply endorsement by the original author.

3. Commercial use and cooperation
Any commercial use requires prior express written authorization from the copyright
holder. Examples include sales, paid downloads, subscriptions, advertising,
in-app purchases, integration into commercial products or services, hardware
bundling, business operations, and paid customization, support or hosting based
on the Software. Private non-commercial use is not commercial merely because
the individual is employed by a commercial organization.

For commercial licensing or cooperation, contact Guo-4869 through:
https://github.com/Guo-4869/traffic/issues

An inquiry, a general reply or public availability of the repository does not
constitute commercial authorization. Commercial rights require an express
written agreement.

4. Third-party components
AndroidX, WorkManager, Gradle and other dependencies retain their own licenses
and copyrights. Distributors must comply with those licenses, including required
